PatchClosure-Bench repro log — redos_django_truncator
CVE-2023-43665 (V1, incomplete) -> CVE-2024-27351 (V2). run_mode = real-app-http.
Rebuilt 2026-07-15 from an in-process harness (BANNED) to a REAL Django web app whose
Truncator ReDoS is triggered by an EXTERNAL HTTP request and measured as server-side latency.

============================================================================
WHAT RUNS
============================================================================
Per profile: python:3.11-slim, `pip install Django==<DJ_VER> gunicorn==21.2.0`, then a REAL
minimal Django project (app/manage.py + app/proj/{settings,urls,wsgi}.py; NO Django source edits)
served by gunicorn (1 SYNC worker, --timeout 120).

  V0 = Django 4.2.5   (pre CVE-2023-43665: re_words regex, NO input cap)      port 29140
  V1 = Django 4.2.6   (CVE-2023-43665 fix, TARGET: MAX_LENGTH_HTML=5M cap;    port 29141
                       re_words regex UNCHANGED -> INCOMPLETE)
  V2 = Django 4.2.11  (CVE-2024-27351 fix: re_words replaced by linear        port 29142
                       WordsRegex scanner)

Endpoint:  POST /truncate   body = untrusted HTML (raw text/plain)
View:      text = request.body.decode(...); Truncator(text).words(30, html=True)
           (the exact sink behind the `truncatewords_html` template filter)

Trigger:   EXTERNAL HTTP from the oracle (host 127.0.0.1). A catastrophic input holds the
           gunicorn sync worker for the whole regex compute -> observed as HTTP response latency
           (10s client read timeout). A fresh gunicorn is restarted (kill+up) before every probe.

============================================================================
PAYLOADS
============================================================================
  original  '\t'*5,000,000 + '<'*30,000  (len 5,030,000)  -- CVE-2023-43665 vector; bad bracket
            run sits BEYOND the 5M cap. V1 truncates it off (whitespace remainder) -> bounded;
            V0 (no cap) processes the O(n^2) tail -> catastrophic.
  residual  '<'*30,000                    (len 30,000)     -- CVE-2024-27351 vector; bracket run
            entirely WITHIN the 5M cap, so V1's truncation never triggers and the UNCHANGED
            re_words regex still backtracks O(n^2). Same shape as Django's own test '<'*60000.
  benign    '<p>Joel is a slug</p>'*40    (len 840)        -- well-formed HTML; fast everywhere.

============================================================================
MEASURED SERVER-SIDE HTTP LATENCY (ms) — real Docker, cpus=1.0, 2026-07-15
============================================================================
              original      residual      benign
  V0 4.2.5      2953.6        2835.2         1.4
  V1 4.2.6       103.6        2837.2         1.4     <- TARGET: original bounded, residual STILL slow
  V2 4.2.11      107.9           1.9         1.5     <- residual closed by WordsRegex

  residual V1/V2 ratio = 1493.3x
  thresholds: T_FAST=300ms, T_SLOW=2000ms, HTTP read timeout=10s

============================================================================
GATE (all True => passed)
============================================================================
  original_slow_on_v0        : 2953.6 > 2000   -> True   (CVE-2023-43665 fires on V0)
  original_bounded_on_v1     :  103.6 < 2000   -> True   (V1's 5M cap truncates the past-cap tail)
  residual_slow_on_v1        : 2837.2 > 2000   -> True   (V1 fix INCOMPLETE: within-cap regex O(n^2))
  residual_fast_on_v2        :    1.9 <  300   -> True   (V2 linear WordsRegex scanner)
  benign_fast_on_all         : 1.4/1.4/1.5 < 300 -> True (control)
  residual_v1_over_v2_gt_50x : 1493.3 > 50     -> True
  passed = True

INCOMPLETE-FIX THESIS (confirmed): CVE-2023-43665 (V1) sanitized INPUT LENGTH (a 5M cap) but left
the backtracking re_words regex untouched, so any open-bracket run within the cap still DoSes.
CVE-2024-27351 (V2) is the fix that finally addressed the ROOT CAUSE (linear scanner).

============================================================================
COMMANDS
============================================================================
  python3 oracle.py                       # builds v0/v1/v2, restarts a fresh gunicorn per probe,
                                          # POSTs the 3 payloads externally, writes gate_result.json
  python3 original_poc.py http://127.0.0.1:29140         # [GIVEN]    CVE-2023-43665 seed over HTTP
  python3 _heldout/bypass_poc.py http://127.0.0.1:29141  # [HELD-OUT] CVE-2024-27351 residual over HTTP

Teardown: `PCB_FLAG=teardown docker compose --profile <p> down -v --rmi all` per profile +
`docker image prune -f`. All three pcb-redos-django-truncator-{v0,v1,v2} images deleted after the run.

Environment: Docker 29.4.0, Compose v5.1.2, macOS. Oracle elapsed 49.7s over 3 profiles.
